  // design: Set pieces part 3 (docs/SET_PIECES_PLAN.md, "The trench and the terrain"). Sunk, not raised: the channel floor is 1.5 m under the level and the ground beside it is the tile's own (earth slabs to the cell edge), so on terrain its floors carve the slot (settle.ts terrainUnderFloors lowers the ground under every floor: a buried carve floor 0.3 m inside the cell edge takes the terrain under the whole trench below the channel, while the cell edge keeps it just under the ground slabs, so the ground outside meets them). Revetment: the walls slot (timber or sandbags by the set piece). Standing in the channel your head is under the 0.6 m parapet; on the fire step (0.75 m) your eyes clear it by 0.25 m; crouched in the channel you are hidden from all round, on the fire step from the front. The fire step stops 0.8 m short of the cell's ends, so a join always has the whole channel clear. Needs terrain: on a map without terrain the ground is drawn at the lowest floor, under the trench (use the raised Military Compound trenches there).
